From: LiuWei <sunflowers0607@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:54:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] claude: a message that ends the turn gives up every call
 still awaited

A call is told by itself, and the message written after it doesn't
have it and ends the turn (the attempt that made the call was cut and
asked again, and the answer is words). No message with that call will
come. Nothing gave it up, so the message became lateID and was left
out, the result after it had no case for that, and the reply never
ended until the client gave up. With a stale lateID from an earlier
turn such a message was told by chance; in a run's first turn it
stalled.

end_turn and stop_sequence come with no call (444 of 444 end_turn rows
in 1,207 real interactive-mode transcripts had none), so a message with
either stop now gives up every call still awaited and counts them in
the log line. A refusal was seen once holding its own call, so any
other stop still gives up nothing.

With this, the turn's last message gives every call up anyway, so
TestClaudeTUIMessageAfterOneWithoutItsCall keeps the give-up of owed
calls on a message that doesn't end the turn pinned.

Tests (TestClaudeTUI*), red at the commit before this one with the
reply never ending: LastMessageWithoutCallFirstTurn,
LastMessageWithoutCallSecondTurn, LastMessageStops (end_turn and
stop_sequence). RefusedMessageWithItsCall and MessageAfterOneWithout
ItsCall pass on both and pin what this mustn't change.

Run: go1.26.10 linux/amd64, -tags nogui, no network but loopback:
go test -count=1 -run '^TestClaudeTUI.*$' ./internal/gateway/ ok
(40 passed). Mutants, each red: end_turn only (LastMessageStops), any
stop but tool_use (RefusedMessageWithItsCall), not logged
(LastMessageWithoutCallSecondTurn), logged but not cleared (three red).
